---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Rename or recolour a tag of the board, or with --remove delete it: its id comes off every object and task card that carries it.
One of --name, -c and --remove is needed; --remove stands alone. It cannot be undone, so it needs -y; without it only the dry run is shown, with the number of objects that carry the tag.

USAGE
  holst board tag <board> <tag> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board whose tag to change
  tag     The tag: its title or id

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws   Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --name text      The new title; another tag of the board cannot have it
  -c, --color color    The new color: a palette token, e.g. indigo5, the color of a new tag
      --remove         Delete the tag; it comes off every object and task card
  -y, --yes            Confirm a risky change; a terminal asks instead; without one only the dry run is shown (exit code 77)
  -n, --dry-run        Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b tag "Roadmap" urgent --name "Urgent!"
  $ holst b tag "Roadmap" urgent -c red5
  $ holst b tag "Roadmap" urgent --remove -y

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
